  "scra_content": {
    "name": "SCRA §3951 (Servicemembers Civil Relief Act)",
    "applies_when": "Tenant (or immediate dependent) is a servicemember in active military service — Army, Navy, Marine Corps, Air Force, Space Force, Coast Guard, or National Guard on federal orders. Also applies to activated Reservists.",
    "effect": "Landlord may not evict servicemember or dependents from primary residence without a court order. Court may: (1) stay eviction proceedings for up to 90 days on application, (2) adjust the rental obligation, or (3) grant other relief as equity requires. Protection applies when the monthly rent does not exceed the threshold adjusted annually for inflation (threshold: $4,073.16/month as of 2024). Before judgment may enter, landlord must file affidavit stating whether defendant is in military service (50 U.S.C. §3931). Failure to file affidavit is a federal misdemeanor. Servicemember who demonstrates material affect on military duty may apply for stay.",
    "statute": "50 U.S.C. §3951; Servicemembers Civil Relief Act (SCRA) §301, Pub. L. 108-189 (2003), as amended",
